Experiment 12: Running JUnit Tests with Maven/Gradle
Aim

To run JUnit test cases using Maven and Gradle build tools.

Theory (Short)

Maven and Gradle are build automation tools used to compile, test, and manage Java projects.
JUnit tests can be executed using Maven and Gradle commands to automate testing and build processes.

Steps
Step 1: Create Maven Project
mvn archetype:generate

Enter:

GroupId: com.devops.lab
ArtifactId: lab12-maven
Packaging: jar
Archetype: maven-archetype-quickstart

Move to folder:

cd lab12-maven
Step 2: Create Calculator.java
src/main/java/com/devops/lab/Calculator.java

Add:

public int subtract(int a, int b) {
    return a - b;
}
Step 3: Create JUnit Test
src/test/java/com/devops/lab/CalculatorTest.java

Add:

assertEquals(5, calculator.subtract(10,5));
Step 4: Run Maven Test
mvn clean test

Output:

BUILD SUCCESS
Tests run: 1
Step 5: Run Gradle Test

Add Gradle configuration:

plugins {
    id 'java'
}

repositories {
    mavenCentral()
}

dependencies {
    testImplementation 'org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter:5.10.0'
    testRuntimeOnly 'org.junit.platform:junit-platform-launcher'
}

test {
    useJUnitPlatform()
}

Run:

gradlew test
